14
00:40:51,360 --> 00:40:52,360
Simple result.

15
00:40:52,360 --> 00:40:57,640
This could be for socks or gold or a job or a date.

16
00:40:57,640 --> 00:41:02,120
Any of these things, just put in more effort and it raises your odds.

17
00:41:02,120 --> 00:41:08,920
Then another assumption, which usually you wouldn't even bother putting into the model,

18
00:41:08,920 --> 00:41:11,840
but you need it to understand the world is just a different searching ability.

19
00:41:11,840 --> 00:41:15,440
So like a professional gold miner has more ability to find gold than I do.

20
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:20,320
You put in a small amount of effort and still it's way more likely to detect it than I am.

21
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:26,920
And then last, normally search theory assumes rational expectations.

22
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:32,560
So on average, people are correct in estimating their probability of finding things, their

23
00:41:32,560 --> 00:41:36,360
