01:12:17,760 --> 01:12:21,880
would be the other way around, then you would be convex.

288
01:12:21,880 --> 01:12:25,200
And then the line would be above the utility function,

289
01:12:25,200 --> 01:12:27,280
indicating that you would rather have the gamble.

290
01:12:27,280 --> 01:12:29,400
You would rather have the gamble.

291
01:12:29,400 --> 01:12:32,280
And of course, if your utility function was a straight line,

292
01:12:32,280 --> 01:12:35,120
then if you draw a line between any two points

293
01:12:35,120 --> 01:12:38,160
in a straight line, you stay on the line,

294
01:12:38,160 --> 01:12:40,080
indicating that you are indifferent.

295
01:12:40,080 --> 01:12:42,760
Indicating that you're indifferent.

296
01:12:42,760 --> 01:12:46,600
Now, a related concept is the certainty equivalence.

297
01:12:46,600 --> 01:12:50,280
So if you're indifferent between a gamble and x star of certainty,

298
01:12:50,280 --> 01:12:52,720
then x star is, by definition, the certainty equivalent

299
01:12:52,720 --> 01:12:54,400
to that gamble.

300
01:12:54,400 --> 01:12:56,520
So think about any gamble and then say,

301
01:12:56,520 --> 01:12:58,080
what is the amount of money you could

302
01:12:58,080 --> 01:12:59,640
have with certainty that would make you indifferent

303
01:12:59,640 --> 01:13:01,600
between that amount and the gamble?

304
01:13:01,600 --> 01:13:05,120
And that is the certainty equivalence element.

305
01:13:05,120 --> 01:13:07,600
And if you think about the risk premium,

306
01:13:07,600 --> 01:13:11,320
the risk premium is just the difference

307
01:13:11,320 --> 01:13:15,360
between the expected value and the certainty equivalence.

308
01:13:18,600 --> 01:13:20,000
So basically, the expected value is

309
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:22,600
above the certainty equivalent, which it normally will be.

310
01:13:22,600 --> 01:13:24,160
Then there's a positive risk premium.

311
01:13:24,160 --> 01:13:27,560
You're willing to pay something to get rid of the risk.

312
01:13:27,560 --> 01:13:29,920
On the other hand, so if you really just love gambling,

