All right, now, adverse selection is economists' favorite argument for health insurance or for insurance regulation in general.

58
01:83:23,000 --> 01:83:34,000
And in particular, the main regulation that this argues for is mandatory insurance.

59
01:83:34,000 --> 01:83:36,000
And again, going back to this case.

60
01:83:36,000 --> 01:83:40,000
Suppose you ordered everyone to sell their companies regardless of their own desires.

61
01:83:40,000 --> 01:83:42,000
You say every company must be sold.

62
01:83:42,000 --> 01:83:44,000
You must divest.

63
01:83:44,000 --> 01:83:45,000
All right?

64
01:83:45,000 --> 01:83:50,000
So in that case, this gets rid of the adverse selection problem, thus by forcing everyone to sell.

65
01:83:50,000 --> 01:83:51,000
All right?

66
01:83:51,000 --> 01:83:56,000
So in that case, they're all going to be sold, and then buyers can know that the average value sold,

67
01:83:56,000 --> 01:84:03,000
the company sold will be 50, and they'll be happy to pay, say, 51, and then all the mutual beneficial deals happen.

68
01:84:03,000 --> 01:84:10,000
And similarly, if we're talking about health insurance, the idea here is that you require everyone to buy,

69
01:84:10,000 --> 01:84:16,000
and this is going to be good or bad for healthy people when they're forced to buy?

70
01:84:16,000 --> 01:84:18,000
Bad.

71
01:84:18,000 --> 01:84:23,000
But so then what is the argument for the regulation?

72
01:84:23,000 --> 01:84:30,000
The argument is that it is a caloric improvement because the gains to the sick people exceed the losses to the healthy people.

73
01:84:30,000 --> 01:84:35,000
And again, if you – from this example, it's clear that can be true.

74
01:84:35,000 --> 01:84:41,000
So basically the idea is that if you force the healthy people in the pool, they're going to be worse off.

75
01:84:41,000 --> 01:84:44,000
Specifically, the healthiest people will definitely be worse off,

76
01:84:44,000 --> 01:84:56,000
but the loss to them is going to be smaller than the gain to the others, and so it's a net social gain, and that is the real story.

77
01:84:56,000 --> 01:85:00,000
All right, and we are now out of time, so we will continue with this next week.


